      "requiresFacing": true,
      "ports": [
        {
          "seq": 1,
          "role": "NOZZLE",
          "defaultEnd": "FL"
        }
      ],
      "note": {
        "en": "A nozzle is a PORT OWNER, not a line component (ADR-010 section 3). It appears in this pack because the port-creation machinery is identical - one template, one port - but its owner_kind is NOZZLE, so it belongs to a piece of equipment rather than to a piping line. This is what lets a pipe-to-nozzle joint use the joints table unchanged.",
        "fa": "نازل مالک پورت است نه کامپوننت خط. در همین بسته می‌آید چون ساز و کار ساخت پورت یکسان است، اما owner_kind آن NOZZLE است و به تجهیز تعلق دارد نه به خط لوله."
      }
    },
    {
      "code": "BOLT",
      "name": {
        "en": "Bolt",
        "fa": "پیچ"
      },
      "category": "FLANGE",
      "sizeRule": "SAME_AS_FIRST",
      "qualifiers": [
        "STUD",
        "MACHINE"
      ],
      "ports": [],
      "note": {
        "en": "Deliberately portless. A bolt does not connect two runs of pipe - it closes a flanged joint. PCF says the same thing: BOLT carries CO-ORDS but no END-POINT, and the format gives it its own UNITS-BOLT-DIA and UNITS-BOLT-LENGTH headers. It is ordered in its own right, with an allowance over the calculated need, so it is a take-off line rather than something derived from the flanges. The qualifier is the fastener style and it is load bearing: a STUD is a headless rod with a nut at each end, measured thread to thread; a MACHINE bolt has an integral head, takes one nut, is measured from under the head, and is permitted by B16.5 only at Class 150 and 300. FlangeBolting reads the style, never a bare nut ratio.",
        "fa": "عمداً بدون پورت. پیچ دو سر لوله را به هم وصل نمی‌کند بلکه یک اتصال فلنجی را می‌بندد. در PCF هم همین است: رکورد BOLT مختصات دارد ولی END-POINT ندارد. کوالیفایر همان سبک بست است: استاد بولت سر ندارد و دو مهره می‌خورد، پیچ ماشینی سر دارد و یک مهره، و B16.5 آن را فقط در کلاس ۱۵۰ و ۳۰۰ مجاز می‌داند."
      }
    },
